  "id": "chimerism",
  "term": "chimerism",
  "definition": "Chimerism is the presence of genetically different cell lineages within one organism, such as after fusion of individuals from the same species. It can increase size, survival, reproduction, and stress tolerance, but it also creates the possibility of competition between those different cell lineages.",
